course: dictionary
lesson: 3594
title: Fielders in the field
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fielder is a player whose team is not batting. Their job is to catch the ball or stop it, so the batter cannot score easily. «Fielders close to the batter wear a helmet or stand further back, because hard shots hit them.» Here, fielders are the players out on the field, not the players holding the bat.
explain: Use the words around fielder to work out its meaning. Phrases like «a good fielder», «outfielder» and «the fielder caught it» give clues: a fielder catches or stops the ball. An outfielder is a fielder who stands further away from the batter.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «The fielder caught it», try "the player whose team is not batting caught it". It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Look at this cricket example: «A cricket ball is very hard, almost like a stone covered in leather, so batters wear a helmet, pads and gloves, and fielders close to the bat wear a helmet or stand back.» The batter and the fielders are on opposite teams, and the clue is that the batter hits and the fielders try to stop the ball.
fact: A fielder is a player whose team is not batting.
fact: Fielders try to catch or stop the ball.
fact: Fielders play in cricket, baseball and rounders.
fact: «A cricket ball is very hard, almost like a stone covered in leather.»
fact: Fielders close to the batter can be hit by hard shots, so they may wear a helmet.
exercise: In cricket, what does a fielder try to do? | *Catch or stop the ball | Hit the ball hard with a bat | Tell the players when to start | Count the runs for the team
exercise: «The fielder caught it, and the batter was out.» Find and copy the word that means the player who is hitting. | pads | fielder | *batter | helmet
exercise: Which team is a fielder on? | *The team that is not batting | Both teams at once | The team that is batting | Neither team
test: Ella says, «The outfielder ran to the edge of the field to catch it.» What is an outfielder? | A helmet worn by players | *A fielder who stands further out on the field | A batter who hits the ball far | A ball made of leather
test: Why do fielders close to the batter wear a helmet? | *Because hard shots may hit them | The sun is very hot | Because they are batting | Because helmets look cool
exam: Read «The fielder caught it, and the team cheered.» Which phrase gives the best meaning for fielder? | *the player whose team is not batting, who catches the ball | the team that hits the ball | a leather ball that is very hard | a kind of bat used in rounders
